@startuml
left to right direction
actor "DMS Administrator" as DMSAdmin
actor "Django superuser" as Superuser
rectangle "APGC DMS — enterprise administration" {
  usecase "Configure document types and workflow models\n[CURRENT: Django Admin perms]" as Configure
  usecase "Manage users / groups / permissions\n[CURRENT: Django Admin + audit]" as Identity
  usecase "Govern role policy and access reviews\n[FUTURE: DMS role]" as Governance
  usecase "View privileged administration audit\n[PARTIAL: admin/organization audit surfaces]" as Audit
  usecase "Bypass document ownership / classification\n[NOT implied; policy decision]" as Bypass
}
DMSAdmin ..> Configure : role-specific grant future
DMSAdmin ..> Identity : role-specific grant future
DMSAdmin ..> Governance : target responsibility
DMSAdmin ..> Audit : target capability
Superuser --> Configure
Superuser --> Identity
Superuser --> Audit
note bottom of Superuser
  Django superuser is an account-level status, not the
  DMS Administrator group. Memo workspace visibility and
  service invariants still apply; do not conflate identities.
end note
@enduml
